# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# An inline if body gives no separate name scope. Its held callable remains
# available after the block; make2(100)'s result applied to (1, 2) is 112.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
int: c 1
if: c = 1
    @: h2 make2(100)
---
int: result h2(1 2)
if: result = 112
    result: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
